{:edb/db-before-t 2072 :edb/db-after-t 2073 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535385 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:15:18.769Z" 13194139535385 true] [17592186157902 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328434 13194139535385 false] [17592186157902 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346953 13194139535385 true] [17592186157902 1100 "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry? Interpret each integral as an ordinary definite integral, using the ordinary improper-integral definition at any interior singularity, rather than a Cauchy principal value.\n\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{4}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$" 13194139535385 true] [17592186157902 1100 "Which of the following integrals has Cauchy principal value zero due to symmetry? For every internal pole, remove an interval of equal radius on its two sides and take the radius to zero. This principal-value convention does not assert convergence of the ordinary improper integral.\n\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{4}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$" 13194139535385 false] [17592186157902 1145 "For an integrable odd function, the ordinary integral over opposite limits is zero. When an interval contains poles, odd symmetry alone does not prove that the ordinary improper integral exists. This question instead specifies Cauchy principal values, with equal exclusions on both sides of each internal pole.\n\nI. The continuous function $\\sin^2 x$ is nonnegative and not identically zero on $[-2,2]$. Its integral is $2-\\frac12\\sin4>0$, so I is not zero.\n\nII. The function $\\tan(2x)$ is odd. Its poles in $(-3,3)$ are $-3\\pi/4,-\\pi/4,\\pi/4,3\\pi/4$. The remaining domain is symmetric when equal intervals are removed about these paired poles, so its integral is zero before taking the limit. Hence the specified principal value is zero. Its ordinary improper integral diverges because the one-sided integrals at each pole do not converge separately.\n\nIII. The function $4\\tan x$ is odd, but $[-2,4]$ is not symmetric. Its internal poles are $-\\pi/2$ and $\\pi/2$. Using the antiderivative $-4\\ln|\\cos x|$ on the continuous pieces, equal two-sided exclusions at each pole cancel their divergent terms. The principal value is\n\n$$4\\ln\\left|\\frac{\\cos2}{\\cos4}\\right|,$$\n\nwhich lies between $-1.81$ and $-1.80$ and is not zero. The ordinary improper integral again diverges.\n\nTherefore, under the stated principal-value convention, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535385 false] [17592186157902 1145 "The ordinary improper-integral definition requires every one-sided integral at each interior singularity to converge separately. Oddness alone cannot establish that a singular integral converges.\n\nI is a proper integral with a nonnegative, nonzero integrand. Using $\\sin^2x=(1-\\cos 2x)/2$ gives\n\n$$\\int_{-2}^{2}\\sin^2x\\,\\mathrm{d}x=2-\\frac{\\sin 4}{2}>0.$$\n\nII has interior poles at $x=\\pm\\pi/4$ and $x=\\pm3\\pi/4$. Near each pole $c$, $\\tan(2x)$ behaves as $-1/(2(x-c))$, so the required one-sided improper integrals diverge. Thus II is undefined as an ordinary improper integral.\n\nIII has interior poles at $x=\\pm\\pi/2$. Near each pole $c$, $4\\tan x$ behaves as $-4/(x-c)$, so its required one-sided improper integrals also diverge. Thus III is undefined as an ordinary improper integral.\n\nTherefore, none of I, II, III evaluates to zero under the stated ordinary-integral interpretation. The correct choice is “None of I, II, III.”\n\nThe source accepted “II only” by applying odd-function symmetry without a stated convergence condition. That answer is valid for II under a separately specified Cauchy principal-value interpretation with symmetric cuts at every interior pole. Under that different convention, III has principal value $4\\ln(|\\cos 2|/|\\cos 4|)\\ne0$. Principal values do not make the ordinary improper integrals converge." 13194139535385 true] [17592186346953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346954 13194139535385 true] [17592186346953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346955 13194139535385 true] [17592186346953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346956 13194139535385 true] [17592186346953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346957 13194139535385 true] [17592186346953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346958 13194139535385 true] [17592186346953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346959 13194139535385 true] [17592186346953 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535385 true] [17592186346953 1041 "selection" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346953 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346959 13194139535385 true] [17592186346953 1110 #uuid "9a60f2b9-1fc5-57d7-9824-fb208d71290c" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346954 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346954 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535385 true] [17592186346954 1111 #uuid "74ceb1f1-5d91-59d9-a6c3-33d82ea8d213" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346955 1034 "III only" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346955 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535385 true] [17592186346955 1111 #uuid "ecdccd09-54f8-5535-8ac3-6041eae29526" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346956 1034 "II only" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346956 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535385 true] [17592186346956 1111 #uuid "9cec89e5-9ea8-5bf1-82db-c0d2bd97ce36" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346957 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346957 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535385 true] [17592186346957 1111 #uuid "48477275-cfb7-59f3-a319-f1cc242363ad" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346958 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346958 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535385 true] [17592186346958 1111 #uuid "2e35dccb-7063-5a4e-b247-b0b7d1551582" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346959 1034 "None of I, II, III" 13194139535385 true] [17592186346959 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535385 true] [17592186346959 1111 #uuid "8211e2d5-b6f8-581d-b838-2ba5b8c96121" 13194139535385 true]] :edb/